{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_013fEBbVWFSY2fFacR5GhT3H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`ai-engineering/answers/02-021-how-evaluate-a-rag-pipeline-ndcg-mrr-precisionk-recall.md`** — the answer note for Q21: *How evaluate a RAG pipeline? NDCG, MRR, precision@k, recall?*\n\n**Key content:**\n- **Two-layer framework**: retrieval metrics (Recall@5, MRR, NDCG, Precision@k) + generation metrics (RAGAS Faithfulness, Answer Relevancy, Context Precision, Context Recall)\n- **Metric selection guide**: MRR for QA (one right answer), NDCG for ranked search (graded relevance), Recall@5 as primary KPI\n- **Eval workflow**: golden dataset (200–500 triples) → offline gate before deploy (block if Recall@5 drops >3pts or Faithfulness <0.8) → async production sampling at 5%\n- **Concrete example**: hybrid search lifted Recall@5 from 61%→73%; cross-encoder reranking lifted Precision@5 from 55%→78% and RAGAS Faithfulness from 0.71→0.86\n- **4 pitfalls**: BLEU/ROUGE wrong for RAG, skipping retrieval layer entirely, ignoring golden dataset build process, not addressing LLM judge cost\n- **Production signals**: deflection rate ≥80%, p95 latency <3s, thumbs-down rate <5%\n\n13 items remaining in the Next queue."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":412,"cache_read_input_tokens":60908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":412,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b88618d-befb-44e5-a8fb-0eb8c82cc2b7","uuid":"fa67d751-a845-4071-b538-b7a5dbc9248f"}
